    {
      "id": "a1-01-l1",
      "title": "Ciao e buongiorno",
      "minutes": 7,
      "goal": "You can greet people and say goodbye, formally and informally.",
      "takeaway": "Ciao is for friends; buongiorno, buonasera and arrivederci are safe with everyone.",
      "exercises": [
        {
          "type": "speak_repeat",
          "id": "a1-01-l1-e01",
          "stage": "warmup",
          "instruction": "Listen, then say it out loud.",
          "text": "Ciao!",
          "translation": "Hi! / Bye!"
        },
        {
          "type": "grammar_note",
          "id": "a1-01-l1-e02",
          "stage": "learn",
          "title": "Salutare",
          "body": "Italians greet by the time of day.\n\n| quando | si dice |\n|---|---|\n| morning, daytime | ==Buongiorno== |\n| afternoon, evening | ==Buonasera== |\n| going to bed | ==Buonanotte== |\n| goodbye (polite) | ==Arrivederci== |\n| hi / bye (friends) | ==Ciao== |\n\n> Use buongiorno and buonasera with strangers, in shops and offices. Ciao is for people you know.",
          "examples": [
            {
              "it": "Buongiorno, signora!",
              "en": "Good morning, madam."
            },
            {
              "it": "Ciao, Marco!",
              "en": "Hi, Marco!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "grammar_note",
          "id": "a1-01-l1-e03",
          "stage": "learn",
          "title": "Come stai?",
          "body": "To ask how someone is, choose **tu** (friends) or **Lei** (polite).\n\n| | informale | formale |\n|---|---|---|\n| ask | Come ==stai==? | Come ==sta==? |\n| answer | Bene, grazie. E ==tu==? | Bene, grazie. E ==Lei==? |\n\n> Lei (the polite *you*) is for strangers, older people and offices.",
          "examples": [
            {
              "it": "Ciao, Anna! Come stai?",
              "en": "Hi, Anna! How are you?"
            },
            {
              "it": "Buongiorno, signor Rossi. Come sta?",
              "en": "Good morning, Mr Rossi. How are you?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listen_choose",
          "id": "a1-01-l1-e04",
          "stage": "practise",
          "instruction": "Listen and choose.",
          "audioText": "Buonasera, signora!",
          "question": "When do you hear this?",
          "options": [
            "In the evening",
            "In the morning",
            "At bedtime"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Buonasera is the greeting for the afternoon and evening."
        },
        {
          "type": "sort_buckets",
          "id": "a1-01-l1-e05",
          "stage": "practise",
          "instruction": "Put each item in the right group.",
          "buckets": [
