    {
      "id": "a1-01-l4",
      "title": "L'alfabeto",
      "minutes": 8,
      "goal": "You can say the Italian letter names and spell your name aloud.",
      "takeaway": "Spell with the letter names; ce / ci and ge / gi are soft, che / chi and ghe / ghi are hard; double letters are held longer.",
      "exercises": [
        {
          "type": "translate",
          "id": "a1-01-l4-e01",
          "stage": "warmup",
          "instruction": "Translate.",
          "direction": "en_it",
          "source": "My name is Anna.",
          "answers": [
            "Mi chiamo Anna."
          ],
          "explanation": "Mi chiamo + name says your name."
        },
        {
          "type": "grammar_note",
          "id": "a1-01-l4-e02",
          "stage": "learn",
          "title": "Come si scrive?",
          "body": "Ask: **Come si scrive?** Say double letters with **doppia**: Anna = a, ==doppia== enne, a.\n\n| lettere | nomi |\n|---|---|\n| A B C D E F G | a, bi, ci, di, e, effe, gi |\n| H I L M N O P | acca, i, elle, emme, enne, o, pi |\n| Q R S T U V Z | qu, erre, esse, ti, u, vu, zeta |",
          "examples": [
            {
              "it": "Si scrive emme, a, erre, ci, o.",
              "en": "It's spelled M-A-R-C-O."
            },
            {
              "it": "Anna: a, doppia enne, a.",
              "en": "Anna: A, double N, A."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "grammar_note",
          "id": "a1-01-l4-e03",
          "stage": "learn",
          "title": "C e G",
          "body": "Before **e / i**, c and g are soft. With **h**, they are hard.\n\n| scritto | suono | esempio |\n|---|---|---|\n| ==ci==, ==ce== | like *ch* | ciao, cena |\n| ==chi==, ==che== | like *k* | chi, che |\n| ==gi==, ==ge== | like *j* | gelato, giorno |\n| ==ghi==, ==ghe== | like *g* in *get* | spaghetti |\n\n> Double letters are held longer: **anno** is not **ano**.",
          "examples": [
            {
              "it": "Ciao, mi chiamo Chiara.",
              "en": "Hi, my name is Chiara."
            },
            {
              "it": "Il gelato e gli spaghetti.",
              "en": "The ice cream and the spaghetti."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "listen_transcribe",
          "id": "a1-01-l4-e04",
          "stage": "practise",
          "instruction": "Listen and type what you hear.",
          "audioText": "Mi chiamo Chiara.",
          "answers": [
            "Mi chiamo Chiara.",
            "Mi chiamo Chiara"
          ],
          "explanation": "Chiara is written with ch because the sound is hard (k).",
          "slow": true
        },
